@5. TRUE IS -1
.
=5. TRUE IS -1
.
.Every flag the library hands back is -1 for true and 0 for false, and
.anything written against it should be too. GUI.OK GUI.ANSWER GUI.STASHED
.STASH.OK SORT.OK MENUVERT.HOTHIT FILE.OK BANKMGR.OK APPSYS.IS.EMULATOR --
.all of them.
.
.That is what a comparison in this compiler evaluates to, so a flag and a
.test read the same way, and it is the value NOT wants: NOT is -x-1, so NOT
.-1 is 0 while NOT 1 is -2, which is still true. IF itself tests non-zero, so
.IF FLAG THEN works either way and IF FLAG = 1 THEN is the spelling that
.breaks.
.
:IF GUI.OK THEN <accepted>            ' yes
:IF NOT GUI.OK THEN <cancelled>       ' yes
:IF GUI.OK = 0 THEN <cancelled>       ' yes
:IF GUI.OK = 1 THEN <accepted>        ' NO -- it is -1
.
.A flag the CALLER sets is read as non-zero, so LINEINPUT.MASK = 1 and
.STASH.MOVE = 1 still work. Write -1 in new code all the same.
.
.Printing one needs STR$ whole. The MID$(STR$(N), 2) idiom strips the leading
.space STR$ puts on a positive number; -1 has no leading space, so that idiom
.eats the minus and prints 1.
